---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="For Data Providers: List Your Feed" activeNav="providers">
  <div style="max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <!-- Hero -->
    <div style="margin-bottom: 3.5rem;">
      <div class="badge badge-blue" style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Phase 3 Marketplace</div>
      <h1 style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem); font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: -0.025em; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
        List Your Feed in the Agent Data Pipe
      </h1>
      <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.6;">
        Data owners, custom filter authors, and analysis creators: sell your feeds directly to agent swarms without building custom MCP servers or handling billing.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- The Problem for Data Owners -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 4rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 800; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        Why Selling Data to Agents is Broken Today
      </h2>
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem;">
        <div class="card">
          <h3 style="font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-rose); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            Integration Friction
          </h3>
          <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem;">
            Every agent developer must write custom connectors, configure per-user credentials, and manage authentication stores.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3 style="font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-rose); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            Context Window Bloat
          </h3>
          <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem;">
            Publishing your own standalone MCP server forces users to burn context window tokens just to register your tool definitions.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3 style="font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-rose); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            Trust & Quality Doubts
          </h3>
          <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem;">
            Buyers have no independent way to verify your latency, uptime, or revision behavior before subscribing.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The Trooth Provider Advantage -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 4rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 800; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        What Trooth Does for Providers
      </h2>

      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.25rem;">
        <div class="card" style="border-left: 4px solid var(--primary);">
          <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; color: var(--primary);">
            1. Zero Integration Overhead
          </h3>
          <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem;">
            You list once as a catalog YAML entry. Any agent connected to Trooth can immediately resolve queries to your endpoint without installing new tools.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card" style="border-left: 4px solid var(--primary);">
          <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; color: var(--primary);">
            2. You Set Your Own Price
          </h3>
          <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem;">
            Providers set their own price per query or per record. Trooth does not price your data. We handle per-request metering and automated payouts.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card" style="border-left: 4px solid var(--primary);">
          <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; color: var(--primary);">
            3. Public Scorecard Included
          </h3>
          <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem;">
            Every listed feed gets the same objective six-dimension scorecard as public sources. Superior freshness and schema stability immediately differentiate your feed. We do not run that scoring ourselves. <a href="https://alexchouck-hash.github.io/modafied-site/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: var(--primary);">Modafied</a> does, and its emblems are shown below exactly as they come.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card" style="border-left: 4px solid var(--primary);">
          <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; color: var(--primary);">
            4. Cryptographic Provenance & Lineage
          </h3>
          <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem;">
            Your responses are signed with Ed25519 envelopes and hashed with SHA-256. Consumers get verifiable audit trails proving the data came from you.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Independent benchmark emblems, served live from Modafied -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 4rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 800; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
        What the Benchmark Actually Says
      </h2>
      <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        These are the live Modafied emblems for the feeds we route to today. They are hotlinked from
        Modafied, not copied here, so they show the current measurement and they change without
        asking us. Every one carries a trace id: click it and you get the exact scorecard digest,
        method version, and band table the grade came from, plus every claim that emblem has made
        before.
      </p>

      <!-- The conflict of interest, stated before the grades rather than under them. -->
      <div class="card" style="border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-amber); margin-bottom: 1.75rem;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.4rem; color: var(--accent-amber);">
          Disclosure, because it matters here
        </h3>
        <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.7;">
          Trooth funds Modafied. That is exactly why this section shows every feed we route to
          rather than the flattering ones: below you will find a C, and two feeds we cannot yet
          measure well enough to grade at all. Modafied runs identical code on every source, takes
          no money from anything it scores, publishes no purchasable emblem of any kind, and will
          score Trooth's own MCP server the same way once it exists. An emblem here is a
          measurement with a date on it, not an endorsement, a certification, or a partnership.
          If a grade falls, the emblem on this page falls with it and we get no notice.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(340px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        <span data-modafied="nws"></span>
        <span data-modafied="usgs-earthquake"></span>
        <span data-modafied="open-meteo"></span>
        <span data-modafied="bls"></span>
        <span data-modafied="fred"></span>
      </div>

      <p style="color: var(--text-subtle); font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.7;">
        A feed reading <em>insufficient data</em> has not been withheld or hidden; it means the
        benchmark does not yet have the samples to grade it, and saying so is the point.
        Method and band table: <a href="https://alexchouck-hash.github.io/modafied-site/method/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: var(--primary);">the published method</a>.
        Resolve any trace id: <a href="https://alexchouck-hash.github.io/modafied-site/trace/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: var(--primary);">the trace resolver</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- How to Submit a Feed -->
    <section class="card" style="margin-bottom: 4rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
        How to Submit a Feed
      </h2>
      <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        Feeds are submitted via open pull requests to the Trooth catalog directory conforming to <code>schema/catalog/v0.1.json</code>:
      </p>

      <pre><code># Example Provider Entry: catalog/sources/custom-finance.yaml
id: "custom-finance"
name: "Acme Real-Time FX"
description: "Sub-second foreign exchange spot rates with settlement guarantees."
endpoints:
  - name: "latest_rates"
    url: "https://api.acme.example/v1/rates"
    method: "GET"
auth:
  type: "bearer"
license:
  spdx: "Commercial"
  url: "https://acme.example/terms"
  redistribution_allowed: true
refresh_cadence: "10s"
declared_lineage:
  role: "primary"
freshness_field: "timestamp"
cost:
  model: "metered"
  rate_limit: "600 requests per minute"</code></pre>

      <div style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
        <a href="https://github.com/alexchouck-hash/trooth-site" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary">
          Submit Catalog Entry via GitHub PR &rarr;
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <!--
    Modafied's emblem renderer. It fetches each feed's attestation and renders the emblem plus its
    trace line, so this page cannot drift from what the benchmark publishes. It sets no cookie,
    stores nothing, and reports nothing back to Modafied; if Modafied is unreachable each slot falls
    back to a plain linked emblem rather than blanking. Source is public and short, read it:
    https://alexchouck-hash.github.io/modafied-site/v1/embed.js
  -->
  <script is:inline defer src="https://alexchouck-hash.github.io/modafied-site/v1/embed.js"></script>
</Layout>
